    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="3.1">
        <head>Cn 1018 3.1</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#kennedy" n="3.1" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="73" ed="#kennedy"/>7 heonan forð læte manna gehwilcne. ge earmne ge eadigne. folcrihtes wurðe beon.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="212" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And heonan forð læte manna gehwilcne, ge earmne ge eadigne, folcrihtes wurðe beon.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#kennedy" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="73" ed="#kennedy"/>And from now on let every man, whether poor or rich, be entitled to his customary rights.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-d"><pb n="213" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And henceforth, all people, both poor and rich, shall be entitled to their legal rights.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="357"><label>source (roman)</label> <ref target="clause:IICn_1-1">II Cn 1.1</ref> <quote>Table 5.4, II Cn 1:1: Cn 1018 3:1  VI Atr 8:1, III Eg 1:1</quote></note>
      </div>
    </body>
